/-! # `#machine_oneout_any` on the parents of a slotless leaf machine child: `callerL`, `callerLN`, `hftByte` (G1, round par/a-11)

The generator `Tools/ShippingOneOutAnyGenCommand.lean` on the three
declarations of the tests whose one callee is a SLOTLESS LEAF MACHINE child,
and — as a comparison of its copied gate branch with `#machine_oneout` — on
one parent of two gate callees whose generated endpoint exists.

## EXPECTED (stated before the build; the command THROWS on another class)

| declaration | callee (kind) | expected | why |
|---|---|---|---|
| `callerL` | `pickByteH` (machine leaf) | PRESENT | `callerL.machine_design_svH_full` exists, built BY HAND (`Tests/Compiler/OneOutCallerLTest.lean`, imported): the statement rebuilt from the GENERATED lemmas must be `isDefEq` it, and the rebuilt proof is kernel-checked as `callerL.machine_design_svH_full_gen` |
| `callerLN` | `pickByteH` (machine leaf) | GENERATED | no endpoint of that name in the imports; `pickByteH.leaf_*` exist from the run on `callerL` and go through the compare path |
| `hftByte` | `Sparkle.IP.Net.HTTP.httpGetByte` (machine leaf, implicit domain binder) | GENERATED | no endpoint of that name in the imports |
| `callerMix` | `pick`, `pickD` (gate) | PRESENT | generated by `#machine_oneout` (`Tests/Compiler/OneOutTwoCalleeTest.lean`, imported): every `callerMix.oneout_*`, `pick.gate_*`, `pickD.gate_*` and lemma statement generated NOW by this file's gate branch must be `isDefEq` the existing one, and the endpoint's record names the same lemmas |
| `callerInner` | — | REFUSED | no `callerInner.machine_ships_hierHR` (the first scope test) |

If a data condition of `callerLN` or `hftByte` is false or too expensive
for the kernel, the line is `ONEOUT ANY f: FAILED (data condition … [name]: …)`
naming it, the command throws (expected GENERATED), nothing is left under
the names, and NO premise counts as removed for that declaration.

NOT TESTED, because no declaration of the tests has the shape: a parent
with one gate callee AND one machine-leaf callee (the generator's per-entry
case split with cases of two kinds), a machine callee that is refused for a
register / calls of its own / no `let` / other outputs (every such parent
of the tests is refused earlier, for `instFields ≠ []`, or has no
`machine_ships_hierHR`).

NAME CLASH, on purpose not hidden: the hand instances
`Tests/Compiler/OneOutCallerLNTest.lean` and
`Tests/Compiler/OneOutHftByteTest.lean` add the SAME endpoint names by
`#machine_design_svH_full`. They are not imported here. A module importing
this file and one of them does not load (the same constant twice). To put
the hand instances in `Tests.AllTests` instead, import them HERE and change
the two expectations to PRESENT (and `existing := true` in their audits).

## SCOPE (binding for any report)

Per declaration, ONE endpoint: a parent WITH a register, the one-output
closing, callees that are gate children or slotless leaf machine children
with the one output `out`. Data conditions decided per declaration are
conditions, not reductions; the run, `MachineDefines`, `EntryDefines`,
`ChildBnd` stay premises; the result depends on the compiler's guards; the
conclusion is about `DesignSV (childMap D.modules) 0 (checkedOptimize b)` —
the module list, not the SV string, not `#sim`. NOT slotless parents, NOT
machine children with registers or calls, NOT several outputs, NOT "all
successful inputs".

UNVERIFIED at the time of writing: this file was not built. -/
namespace Tests.Compiler.OneOutAnyFamilyTest
open Lean Meta Elab Command

/-- The six lemmas the generator leaves under `f`. -/
def lemmasOf (f : Name) : List Name :=
  [`machine_factsH, `machine_outsH, `machine_portsRawH, `machine_portsShippedH,
   `machine_hierTypedH, `machine_designFullH].map (f ++ ·)

/-- The data conditions the generator leaves under `f`. -/
def condsOf (f : Name) : List Name :=
  [`oneout_callsOk, `oneout_slotLen, `oneout_domB, `oneout_insts, `oneout_instFields,
   `oneout_nomem, `oneout_slots, `oneout_outChars,
   `oneout_kidIns, `oneout_callArgs, `oneout_entries].map (f ++ ·)

/-- The parent's data conditions the default path no longer decides (par/r-5:
`outTy_of_core` / `outScalar_of_core` at the run's `hcore`, `entry`). -/
def readerOf (f : Name) : List Name :=
  [`oneout_outTy, `oneout_outScalar].map (f ++ ·)

/-- What the generator leaves under a machine-leaf callee. -/
def leafOf (c : Name) : List Name :=
  [`leaf_gate, `leaf_calls, `leaf_dom, `leaf_ss, `leaf_insts, `leaf_outTy, `leaf_outChars,
   `leaf_outScalar, `leaf_lets, `leaf_slots, `leaf_one, `leaf_outW, `leaf_slotless].map (c ++ ·)

/-- What the generator leaves under a gate callee. -/
def gateOf (c : Name) : List Name :=
  [`gate_full, `gate_ports, `gate_kidK, `gate_width].map (c ++ ·)

/-- The audit of one declaration after `#machine_oneout_any_try`: SKIPPED
with a log line where no endpoint was generated (the outcome's class was
asserted by the command). -/
def auditAny (f : Name) (machKids gateKids : List Name) (existing : Bool) : MetaM Unit := do
  let full := f ++ `machine_design_svH_full
  let facts := f ++ `machine_factsH
  let old := f ++ `machine_design_svHR
  unless (← getEnv).contains full && (← getEnv).contains facts do
    logInfo m!"ONEOUT ANY FAMILY {f}: no generated endpoint — premise list, axiom audit and goal gap SKIPPED; no premise of {old} counts as removed for {f}"
    return
  for n in readerOf f do
    if (← getEnv).contains n then
      throwError "{n}: generated — the default path takes it from the reader (par/r-5)"
  Tests.Compiler.OneOutLeafAudit.audit "ONEOUT ANY FAMILY" f machKids gateKids (lemmasOf f)
    (condsOf f ++ machKids.flatMap leafOf ++ gateKids.flatMap gateOf ++
      [``Tools.ShippingLeafOneOutGen.gateCallsOk_parts,
       ``Tools.ShippingLeafOneOutGen.leaf_outWidth])
    existing
    (Tests.Compiler.OneOutLeafAudit.scopeOf f
      s!"for {f}: {f}.oneout_callsOk, _slotLen, _domB, _insts, _instFields, _nomem, _slots (the parent has a register), _outChars, _callArgs at the numerals of {f}.oneout_kidIns, _entries (per entry: the callee, its argument widths, the result binder's width); for each machine-leaf callee c in {machKids}: c.leaf_gate (gateCallsOk at nIn), _calls, _dom, _ss, _insts, _outTy, _outChars, _outScalar, _lets, _slots, _one, _outW, with its generated machine_ok / machine_body / machine_closes; for each gate callee in {gateKids}: gate_width and what #gate_child left"
      "a parent mixing a gate callee and a machine-leaf callee (no test declaration)")

/-- A refused declaration has nothing under the generator's names. -/
def leftNothing (f : Name) : MetaM Unit := do
  for n in [f ++ `machine_design_svH_full, f ++ `machine_factsH, f ++ `oneout_callsOk] do
    if (← getEnv).contains n then
      throwError "{n}: left behind by a refused generation"
  logInfo m!"ONEOUT ANY FAMILY: {f} REFUSED, nothing left under its names."

end Tests.Compiler.OneOutAnyFamilyTest

